\f0\b\fs48 \cf0 \strokec2 6. DATABASE\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 Use PostgreSQL.\
The current production baseline should use a supported PostgreSQL release.\
Prefer PostgreSQL 18.x unless the hosting environment imposes a justified compatibility constraint.\
Use Flyway for every schema change.\
Never manually modify production database schema.\
Never rely on Hibernate automatic schema generation in production.\
Production:\
spring.jpa.hibernate.ddl-auto=validate\
Development may use validation as well.\
Every schema change must have a migration.\
Example:\
V1__create_users.sql\
V2__create_properties.sql\
V3__create_investments.sql\
etc.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \strokec3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa321\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs48 \cf0 \strokec2 7. DATABASE DESIGN\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 Design the database around the domain rather than around screens.\
Core entities should include concepts such as:\
User\
Role\
Permission\
Property\
PropertyImage\
PropertyDocument\
InvestmentOpportunity\
Investment\
InvestorPosition\
Transaction\
Distribution\
DistributionAllocation\
Portfolio\
CompanyFundingRound\
CompanyFundingContribution\
Country\
Currency\
AuditLog\
Notification\
RiskDisclosure\
LegalDocument\
Payment\
PaymentAttempt\
IdempotencyKey\
The exact model may evolve after inspecting the project.\
Do not create unnecessary tables.\
Avoid premature microservices.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \strokec3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa321\partightenfactor0

