\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 Use asymmetric signing where appropriate.\
Do not hard-code production secrets or private keys into Git.\
Private signing keys must come from secure deployment configuration/secrets.\
Never commit:\
.env\
private keys\
JWT secrets\
database passwords\
payment secrets\
API keys\
cloud credentials\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \strokec3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa321\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs48 \cf0 \strokec2 15. AUTHORIZATION\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 Authentication answers:\
"Who are you?"\
Authorization answers:\
"What are you allowed to do?"\
Implement both.\
Roles may include:\
USER\
ADMIN\
OPERATOR\
COMPLIANCE\
Additional roles may be added later.\
Users must only access resources they are authorized to access.\
Example:\
GET /api/v1/portfolio/me\
must return the authenticated user's portfolio.\
A user must NEVER be able to retrieve another user's portfolio simply by changing:\
/users/\{id\}\
in the URL.\
Enforce ownership at the backend.\
Never trust frontend authorization.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \strokec3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa321\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs48 \cf0 \strokec2 16. API ARCHITECTURE\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 All APIs must be versioned.\
Base path:\
/api/v1\
Examples:\
/api/v1/auth/login\
/api/v1/auth/register\
/api/v1/users/me\
/api/v1/properties\
/api/v1/properties/\{id\}\
/api/v1/investment-opportunities\
/api/v1/investments\
/api/v1/portfolio\
/api/v1/portfolio/me\
/api/v1/transactions\
/api/v1/distributions\
/api/v1/documents\
/api/v1/notifications\
/api/v1/admin/properties\
/api/v1/admin/investments\
Keep endpoints RESTful.\
Do not create random endpoint naming conventions.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \strokec3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa321\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs48 \cf0 \strokec2 17. API CONTRACT IS THE SOURCE OF TRUTH\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 The frontend and backend must communicate through explicitly defined DTOs.\
Never expose JPA entities directly through controllers.\
Use:\
Request DTO\
Service\
Domain/entity\
Repository\
Response DTO\
Do not return entities directly from REST endpoints.\
Document API contracts using OpenAPI.\
Whenever an API changes:\
