\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Verify serialization/deserialization.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 Never allow frontend and backend contracts to drift.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \strokec3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa321\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs48 \cf0 \strokec2 18. API RESPONSE FORMAT\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 Use a consistent response/error structure.\
For errors, return structured information such as:\
timestamp\
status\
errorCode\
message\
path\
validationErrors\
Do not expose stack traces or internal implementation details to clients.\
Example conceptual error:\
\{\
"status": 400,\
"errorCode": "VALIDATION_ERROR",\
"message": "The investment amount is invalid.",\
"validationErrors": [...]\
\}\
Do not return raw Java exceptions.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \strokec3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa321\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs48 \cf0 \strokec2 19. GLOBAL ERROR HANDLING\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 Implement centralized backend error handling.\
Use appropriate HTTP status codes:\
400 validation\
401 authentication\
403 authorization\
404 resource not found\
409 conflict\
422 business-rule violation where appropriate\
429 rate limit\
500 unexpected server error\
Never leak internal exceptions.\
Log the internal error server-side with a correlation/request ID.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \strokec3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa321\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs48 \cf0 \strokec2 20. API SECURITY\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 Implement:\
CORS\
CSRF strategy appropriate to the authentication architecture\
security headers\
rate limiting where appropriate\
request validation\
maximum request sizes\
safe file-upload validation\
SQL injection protection through parameterized/JPA queries\
authorization checks\
audit logging\
secure cookie configuration where cookies are used\
HTTPS in production\
Do not allow:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls12\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 origins\
in production unless there is an explicit and justified reason.\
Development and production CORS configuration must be separate.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \strokec3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa321\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs48 \cf0 \strokec2 21. FILE UPLOADS\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 Users may eventually upload:\
identity documents\
property documents\
legal documents\
financial documents\
Do NOT store sensitive documents casually inside the application container filesystem.\
Design a storage abstraction.\
Example:\
DocumentStorageService\
with a local implementation for development and object-storage implementation for production.\
Validate:\
file type\
file size\
extension\
MIME type\
filename\
content where appropriate\
Never trust the original filename.\
Do not make sensitive documents publicly accessible.\
Use authorization-controlled access.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \strokec3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa321\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs48 \cf0 \strokec2 22. FRONTEND ARCHITECTURE\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 Use feature-oriented organization.\
Example:\
src/\
app/\
components/\
features/\
auth/\
properties/\
investments/\
portfolio/\
transactions/\
distributions/\
documents/\
admin/\
lib/\
api/\
hooks/\
schemas/\
types/\
stores/\
routes/\
styles/\
Do not put the entire application into App.tsx.\
Keep components focused.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \strokec3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa321\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs48 \cf0 \strokec2 23. FRONTEND API LAYER\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 Create ONE centralized API client.\
Example conceptual structure:\
apiClient\
authApi\
userApi\
propertyApi\
investmentApi\
portfolioApi\
transactionApi\
distributionApi\
documentApi\
adminApi\
Do not make raw fetch/axios requests randomly throughout components.\
React components should call typed API functions/hooks.\
This is extremely important.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \strokec3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa321\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs48 \cf0 \strokec2 24. API BASE URL\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 Use environment configuration.\
Example:\
VITE_API_BASE_URL\
But remember:\
VITE_* variables are public and become part of the frontend build.\
Therefore:\
NEVER put secrets into VITE_* variables.\
Only public configuration may exist there.\
Examples:\
VITE_API_BASE_URL={\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://api.example.com/"}}{\fldrslt \cf4 \ul \ulc4 \strokec4 https://api.example.com}}\
is acceptable.\
Database passwords, private API keys, JWT private keys, payment secrets, etc. are NOT.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \strokec3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa321\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs48 \cf0 \strokec2 25. TANSTACK QUERY\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 Use TanStack Query for server state.\
Use it for:\
properties\
portfolio\
investments\
transactions\
distributions\
notifications\
user data\
Do not duplicate server state unnecessarily in Zustand.\
Use Zustand for genuine client state such as:\
UI preferences\
sidebar state\
temporary client workflow state\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \strokec3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa321\partightenfactor0

