{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://contributing.md/"}}{\fldrslt \cf4 \ul \ulc4 \strokec4 CONTRIBUTING.md}}\
Each document should remain accurate.\
README should explain:\
local development\
environment variables\
database startup\
frontend startup\
backend startup\
testing\
Docker\
production deployment\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \strokec3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa321\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs48 \cf0 \strokec2 89. ENVIRONMENT EXAMPLE\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 Provide:\
.env.example\
with placeholders.\
Never put real credentials in it.\
Example:\
POSTGRES_DB=rrestate\
POSTGRES_USER=rrestate\
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=CHANGE_ME\
DATABASE_URL=...\
JWT_ISSUER=...\
JWT_PRIVATE_KEY=...\
VITE_API_BASE_URL={\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://localhost:8080/"}}{\fldrslt \cf4 \ul \ulc4 \strokec4 http://localhost:8080}}\
The production environment must use completely separate values.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \strokec3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa321\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs48 \cf0 \strokec2 90. GIT\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 Maintain clean Git history.\
Do not commit:\
.env\
.env.local\
secrets\
build artifacts\
node_modules\
IDE files\
database dumps\
private keys\
uploaded user documents\
Use a proper .gitignore.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \strokec3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa321\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs48 \cf0 \strokec2 91. CODE QUALITY\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 Prefer:\
clear names\
small focused methods\
strong typing\
explicit domain concepts\
simple architecture\
predictable behavior\
meaningful exceptions\
good tests\
Avoid:\
god classes\
massive controllers\
business logic inside React components\
business logic inside repositories\
duplicated API calls\
magic strings\
magic numbers\
copy-paste architecture\
unnecessary abstractions\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \strokec3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa321\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs48 \cf0 \strokec2 92. ERROR PREVENTION\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 Before considering a feature complete, verify:\
Frontend compiles.\
TypeScript passes.\
Backend compiles.\
Backend tests pass.\
Integration tests pass.\
Database migrations work from a clean database.\
Docker builds.\
Docker Compose starts.\
Health checks pass.\
Frontend can communicate with backend.\
Authentication works.\
Authorization works.\
CORS works.\
Production configuration does not expose secrets.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \strokec3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa321\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs48 \cf0 \strokec2 93. FINAL DEFINITION OF DONE\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 A feature is NOT complete merely because the UI exists.\
A feature is complete only when:\
DATABASE\
\uc0\u8595 \
BACKEND DOMAIN\
\uc0\u8595 \
SERVICE\
\uc0\u8595 \
API\
\uc0\u8595 \
API CONTRACT\
\uc0\u8595 \
FRONTEND API CLIENT\
\uc0\u8595 \
QUERY/STATE\
\uc0\u8595 \
UI\
\uc0\u8595 \
VALIDATION\
\uc0\u8595 \
ERROR HANDLING\
\uc0\u8595 \
SECURITY\
\uc0\u8595 \
TESTS\
\uc0\u8595 \
DOCKER\
\uc0\u8595 \
DEPLOYMENT\
all work together.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \strokec3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa321\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs48 \cf0 \strokec2 94. CRITICAL RULE\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 Always maintain a single source of truth.\
If you change:\
database\
update backend.\
If you change backend API:\
update OpenAPI.\
If you change API:\
update frontend types/client.\
If you change authentication:\
update frontend authentication flow.\
If you change financial logic:\
update tests and portfolio calculations.\
If you change environment configuration:\
update Docker and documentation.\
Never leave half-integrated functionality.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \strokec3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa321\partightenfactor0

